@startuml
title Activity Diagram: UC-04 Manage Stocks

|Staff/Admin|
start
:[Step 1.0] Select "Manage Stocks" from Admin Panel Dashboard;

|System|
:[Step 1.1] Retrieve and display current stock levels, low-stock alerts, and item logs;

|Staff/Admin|
:[Step 2.0] Review current stock levels for products and raw ingredients;
:[Step 3.0] Input new stock shipments, adjust quantities manually, or update low-stock thresholds;
:[Step 4.0] Save the stocks updates;

|System|
:[Step 4.1] Validate inputs;
if (Inputs valid and non-negative?) then (Yes)
    :[Step 4.1] Record the updated stock quantities in the database;
    :[Step 4.1] Refresh the stocks view and display a confirmation message;
    if (Quantity below set threshold?) then (Yes)
        :[Step 3.3] Flag items as "Out of Stock" or trigger low-stock notifications;
    else (No)
    endif
else (No)
    :[Exc 4.1.1] Highlight the invalid field, display an error message, and prevent saving until corrected;
endif

|System|
if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Placement)
    :[Step 3.1] Automatically check stock availability during checkout process;
    if (Sufficient stock?) then (Yes)
        :Proceed with order;
    else (No)
        :[Exc 2.1.1] Flag the order item and notify customer with substitute or cancellation options;
    endif
else
    if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Confirmation)
        :[Step 3.2] Automatically deduct reserved quantities from stocks;
        if (Quantity drops below threshold?) then (Yes)
            :[Step 3.3] Trigger low-stock notifications or flag items as "Out of Stock";
        else (No)
        endif
    else
        if (Order Event or Sync Occurs?) then (Order Cancellation)
            :[Step 3.2] Automatically release reserved stock back into inventory;
        else (Third-Party Sync Failure)
            :[Exc 4.1.2] Log the error and alert Staff/Admin to manually reconcile the stock count;
        endif
    endif
endif

|Staff/Admin|
stop

@enduml
